ssues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Fall back to the default resolved-status set when the configured list is EMPTY as well as unset/ConfigError (mirror DC's `... if reconciler.resolved_statuses else DEFAULT`), since `_as_str_list` coerces `[]`/`[\"\"]` to an empty list without raising.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan step 2: 'keeping module-level RESOLVED_STATUS_NAMES as the fallback when config is unset or malformed (ConfigError)'","_config_coercion.py:86-104 `_as_str_list`/`_as_str_tuple` drop empty/blank entries and return `[]` WITHOUT raising ConfigError, so `resolved_statuses = []` (or `[\"\"]`) is neither unset (default_factory only fires when the key is absent) nor a ConfigError.","DC guards exactly this: settings.py:102-106 `frozenset(reconciler.resolved_statuses) if reconciler.resolved_statuses else DEFAULT_RESOLVED_STATUSES` — an empty list falls back to the default.","Sibling Cloud resolver acli_subprocess.py:48-65 `_acli_call_timeout` also falls back on a non-positive value, not only on ConfigError — the established Cloud pattern is 'empty/degenerate value -> default'."],"finding":"The plan's fallback condition ('config is unset or malformed (ConfigError)') omits the empty-list case, so an explicit `jira.resolved_statuses = []` binds an empty set and misclassifies every resolved issue as PRESENT_FILTERED — the exact bug the story fixes, inverted.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f32fc7ea6fe3f2c9c","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 2 / Acceptance criteria (fallback behavior)","norm_id":"n97def83396fcf6ed","priority":0.33,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A Cloud tenant sets `jira.resolved_statuses = []` (e.g. to 'clear' it) or a value that coerces to empty like `[\"\"]`: the classifier's membership test never matches, so every still-present issue is classified PRESENT_FILTERED and no issue is ever PRESENT_RESOLVED."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"In step 2, resolve as: `configured = load_config().jira.resolved_statuses` inside a `try/except ConfigError`, then bind `frozenset(configured) if configured else RESOLVED_STATUS_NAMES` — so unset, malformed (ConfigError), AND explicitly-empty all fall back to the module default, matching settings.py:102-106. Update the empty-config-unset AC accordingly.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v4","material_fingerprint":"88891c8b2df72e98","metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":1379549,"cache_write_tokens":326215,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":601.5,"input_tokens":1722759,"llm_calls":28,"llm_ms":154230.7,"output_tokens":25557,"tot